Subject: arm64: dts: sun50i-h616: add #sound-dai-cells to the HDMI node

The DW-HDMI controller is an ASoC codec provider: a machine node that
references it with `sound-dai = <&hdmi>` needs `#sound-dai-cells` on the
target, otherwise of_parse_phandle_with_args() fails and the sunxi
machine driver (allwinner,sunxi-snd-mach) falls back to snd-soc-dummy —
the card comes up, but every sample is dropped.

Observed on Orange Pi Zero 3 (H618), kernel 7.0.14:

  OF: /soc/ahub1_mach/soundcard-mach,codec: could not get #sound-dai-cells
      for /soc/hdmi@6000000
  /proc/asound/card1/pcm0p/info
  id: ahub_plat-snd-soc-dummy-dai snd-soc-dummy-dai-0

The property is set at the SoC level, like the H6 node gets it from the
hdmi-audio patch set (0010-arm64-dts-allwinner-h6-Add-hdmi-sound-card):
every H616/H618 board that enables `&hdmi` needs it, and the node itself
is introduced by 0042-arm64-dts-allwinner-h616-Add-display-pipeline,
which never carried it.

